                        "source_sense_id": "368ad74b-4449-3648-928e-a41c83032c46",
                        "target_lang_word": "fairly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fairly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "30c1376f-6026-3f07-bd86-9b64673464cb",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a fair manner; fair; not biased or skewed or favouring a certain party"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e14d5de7-1945-4af2-acd9-37982ec4b99a",
                                                "sense_id": "30c1376f-6026-3f07-bd86-9b64673464cb",
                                                "text": "A jury is expected to ensure that the accused is fairly judged."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf90a210-72a6-39e9-8810-bdcc962bfd47",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Favorably; auspiciously; commodiously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f50afb4-e383-4829-9c0f-8104cff0792f",
                                                "sense_id": "cf90a210-72a6-39e9-8810-bdcc962bfd47",
                                                "text": "a town fairly situated for foreign trade"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "130bf230-958f-3fd4-a24f-650eda48cc47",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Honestly; properly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "210bc651-8a2f-4d51-9588-b519d3ed18dc",
                                                "sense_id": "130bf230-958f-3fd4-a24f-650eda48cc47",
                                                "text": "Consumer laws aim to have consumers fairly treated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f53d7ce9-d6b8-4064-8cec-59a846b4f844",
                                                "sense_id": "130bf230-958f-3fd4-a24f-650eda48cc47",
                                                "text": "10. You will be civil and attentive to passengers, giving proper assistance to ladies and children getting in or out, and never start the car before passengers are fairly received or landed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bc1081c-2b3f-4072-9c03-132e39834dec",
                                                "sense_id": "130bf230-958f-3fd4-a24f-650eda48cc47",
                                                "text": "They burned the old gun that used to stand in the dark corner up in the garret, close to the stuffed fox that always grinned so fiercely. Perhaps the reason why he seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. Otherwise his pelt would not have been so perfect. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2617c130-8907-3ec4-bc5a-6387ea19494e",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Softly; quietly; gently."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b47b1ece-999f-357f-b288-57cdcf86b09f",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Partly, not fully; somewhat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bf0b464-a081-4d93-acc8-ea61dba26383",
                                                "sense_id": "b47b1ece-999f-357f-b288-57cdcf86b09f",
                                                "text": "The weather this weekend will be fairly dry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a12ab48-8bb8-42ae-ac5a-4b1031a4eda6",
                                                "sense_id": "b47b1ece-999f-357f-b288-57cdcf86b09f",
                                                "text": "My hopes wa'n't disappointed. I never saw clams thicker than they was along them inshore flats. I filled my dreener in no time, and then it come to me that 'twouldn't be a bad idee to get a lot more, take 'em with me to Wellmouth, and peddle 'em out. Clams was fairly scarce over that side of the bay and ought to fetch a fair price."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "752582b5-b8eb-4852-8141-fea86bd6caa2",
                                                "sense_id": "b47b1ece-999f-357f-b288-57cdcf86b09f",
                                                "text": "The dawn of the oil age was fairly recent. Although the stuff was used to waterproof boats in the Middle East 6,000 years ago, extracting it in earnest began only in 1859 after an oil strike in Pennsylvania. The first barrels of crude fetched $18 (around $450 at today’s prices). It was used to make kerosene, the main fuel for artificial lighting after overfishing led to a shortage of whale blubber."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b30da7c4-0533-3b02-a381-4491efcb3915",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Almost; practically."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "140ea9e9-fab6-40b9-95ad-f36cabbe51cf",
                                                "sense_id": "b30da7c4-0533-3b02-a381-4491efcb3915",
                                                "text": "We quadrilled, waltzed, and conversed, in all of which my clever partner excelled; and her charms, combined with the excellent champagne I imbibed, fairly dazzled my imagination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53b35f19-b4a8-4807-b841-bf89e264bc24",
                                                "sense_id": "b30da7c4-0533-3b02-a381-4491efcb3915",
                                                "text": "Betty grew so nervous and frightened, that she fairly bawled to her colleague, Moggy, and told her she would not stay in the room unless she sat up all night with her."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da6cf2c5-73f2-47e5-83d2-50ed9cab832b",
                                                "sense_id": "b30da7c4-0533-3b02-a381-4491efcb3915",
                                                "text": "I remember the sudden drop in the note of the station bell, as we roar through, perhaps with 16 coaches; sweep up to milepost 9½, and then, with increasing thunder from the exhaust, fairly rush the fells at Milnthorpe at the foot of the climb to Grayrigg, until the steady thunderous beat re-echoes past Mosedale Hall, still at 40 m.p.h."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef347b51-17db-3239-be83-a69dbc10431a",
                                        "entry_id": "c49af43a-fb3c-397f-9e8f-187cb3ec3ec7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of handwriting: neatly and legibly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81a713c7-8a4d-48dc-8579-2102268dad31",
                                                "sense_id": "ef347b51-17db-3239-be83-a69dbc10431a",
                                                "text": "That Pen, which now writes blottingly, might be well made at first, and will write fairly again […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd2eeb90-8231-4139-8982-0ab26d551afa",
                                                "sense_id": "ef347b51-17db-3239-be83-a69dbc10431a",
                                                "text": "I was at the Mathematical School, where the Maſter taught his Pupils after a Method ſcarce imaginable to us in Europe. The Propoſition and Demonſtration were fairly written on a thin Wafer, with Ink compoſed of a Cephalick Tincture. This the Student was to ſwallow upon a faſting Stomach, and for three days following eat nothing but Bread and Water. As the Wafer digeſted, the Tincture mounted to his Brain, bearing the Propoſition along with it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "935cd4d1-850b-4696-84bf-34a50a3f236e",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea6575a5-e7a0-3502-bb4c-74a96f1a870d",
                        "source_sense_id": "368ad74b-4449-3648-928e-a41c83032c46",
                        "target_lang_word": "justly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "justly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "480d0f42-325f-3eec-9eb3-649b4df1cf26",
                                        "entry_id": "673e195d-4bb9-396f-a507-ca2accdc3237",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a just or fair manner; rightfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fdcea92-28e7-4d8a-9445-49980099386e",
                                                "sense_id": "480d0f42-325f-3eec-9eb3-649b4df1cf26",
                                                "text": "His valor, wisdom, and justice made him justly popular, but caused him to be regarded with suspicion at Rome."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d45cc367-5b84-41d1-b2b9-bde6f369569d",
                                                "sense_id": "480d0f42-325f-3eec-9eb3-649b4df1cf26",
                                                "text": "Mention must be made of the Valdres Folk Museum, situated just outside the town—one of those fascinating open-air museums for which Scandinavia is justly famed, to which have been transplanted a number of ancient buildings, such as farmhouses and storehouses, full of appropriate furniture, costumes and other exhibits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06386027-b66a-3935-9d60-13d0504ec42d",
                                        "entry_id": "673e195d-4bb9-396f-a507-ca2accdc3237",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With a just or fair use of language; with good reason, properly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1997e5aa-b073-4876-ba67-06c95c2fa49e",
                                                "sense_id": "06386027-b66a-3935-9d60-13d0504ec42d",
                                                "text": "But the city on the River Clyde can justly claim to have turned the tide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5982e073-52ca-39c0-9734-fdf0af3a8610",
                                        "entry_id": "673e195d-4bb9-396f-a507-ca2accdc3237",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With great precision; accurately, exactly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b7e8398-00a3-4e11-8b0f-7464487149ad",
                                                "sense_id": "5982e073-52ca-39c0-9734-fdf0af3a8610",
                                                "text": "It is a pleasant imagination to conceive a spirit iustly ballanced betweene two equall desires."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "106f9ed1-7fa5-4810-a5b4-0e15e80696be",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea6575a5-e7a0-3502-bb4c-74a96f1a870d",
                        "source_sense_id": "368ad74b-4449-3648-928e-a41c83032c46",
                        "target_lang_word": "fair and square",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fair and square",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66ae37d5-c727-3a85-be31-0d395337c725",
                                        "entry_id": "c71a555e-7782-3947-a101-bfd9cdf4c166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Totally fairly and undoubtedly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0269063-a3cc-4271-ace6-203fa7385d70",
                                                "sense_id": "66ae37d5-c727-3a85-be31-0d395337c725",
                                                "text": "We won the game fair and square."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f995c2eb-afeb-37d9-a6fb-54f990a09825",
                                        "entry_id": "c71a555e-7782-3947-a101-bfd9cdf4c166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Within the applicable rules."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a49a5e2f-53ec-4db6-bb73-8e25a1c21318",
                                                "sense_id": "f995c2eb-afeb-37d9-a6fb-54f990a09825",
                                                "text": "He said they give licenses now to steal — steal folks'es senses away, and then they would steal every thing else, and murder, and tear round into every kind of wickedness. But he didn't ask that. He wanted things done fair and square: he jest wanted to steal horses. He was goin' West, and he thought he could do a good business, and lay up something. If he had a license, he shouldn't be afraid of bein' shot up, or shot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68ad8857-22f5-4172-87e3-fedcf71ea564",
                                                "sense_id": "f995c2eb-afeb-37d9-a6fb-54f990a09825",
                                                "text": "They had crawled in and staked the land and stood ready to shoot those of us who came in, fair and square, in the Run."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59b9dc34-872f-460c-b3aa-7be47824c291",
                                                "sense_id": "f995c2eb-afeb-37d9-a6fb-54f990a09825",
                                                "text": "For the \"Most Accurate Assessment of an International Situation\" the unanimous winner is the Republican U.S. Senate hopeful from California, S.E. Hayakawa. He said, \"Of course we should keep the Panama Canal, we stole it fair and square.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "331d787e-4d47-310b-b872-c5aed685b368",
                                        "entry_id": "c71a555e-7782-3947-a101-bfd9cdf4c166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In all fairness; equitably."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53031121-8824-4f42-9ff7-afaf795d6737",
                                                "sense_id": "331d787e-4d47-310b-b872-c5aed685b368",
                                                "text": "\"Have it out with him to-night. Fair and square. Out he goes, Edmund, neck and crop. Out, by thunder.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fair and square",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3fe8c60-bd69-3063-aa54-2e3c9bc97160",
                                        "entry_id": "704536fd-11d0-3854-97c5-5e56a3875871",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unquestionably fair."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "346c403e-9c96-46f4-805b-75ed9d8f53ed",
                                                "sense_id": "c3fe8c60-bd69-3063-aa54-2e3c9bc97160",
                                                "text": "“[…] I always liked you Joe, and stood up for you, too. Don’t you remember? You won’t tell, will you Joe?” And the poor creature dropped on his knees before the stolid murderer, and clasped his appealing hands. / “No, you’ve always been fair and square with me, Muff Potter, and I won’t go back on you.—There, now, that’s as fair as a man can say.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d180d0f-e0a4-451d-a9bc-17cb0f1041f6",
                                                "sense_id": "c3fe8c60-bd69-3063-aa54-2e3c9bc97160",
                                                "text": "It was a fair and square deal. We won. And we won in the Senate. And it's in the bill. And I didn't think we could beat them, but we did."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a40cfc46-3bff-49ca-ba47-b46e24609811",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea6575a5-e7a0-3502-bb4c-74a96f1a870d",
                        "source_sense_id": "368ad74b-4449-3648-928e-a41c83032c46",
                        "target_lang_word": "justement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "justement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fcdf97df-fd4f-38c2-98a9-41021890dc90",
                                        "entry_id": "63511c68-1d15-3282-8ec9-bbc5e0f13dc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Avec justice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fcfdf7cf-b3a7-4dda-a5ec-4bdaadd4b6e5",
                                                "sense_id": "fcdf97df-fd4f-38c2-98a9-41021890dc90",
                                                "text": "Il a jugé justement. - Il a agi justement. - Il a été puni justement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5b8898a-8fad-383e-b1dc-b5b761fd3aa4",
                                        "entry_id": "63511c68-1d15-3282-8ec9-bbc5e0f13dc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dans la juste proportion, ni plus ni moins qu’il ne faut, précisément."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41b964de-d242-45bb-b5b4-759a4978841c",
                                                "sense_id": "d5b8898a-8fad-383e-b1dc-b5b761fd3aa4",
                                                "text": "Voilà justement ce qui vous manque. - Vous arrivez justement à l’heure qu’il faut. - C’est justement cette explication que je désirais."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16696b34-3806-4730-a847-a630141dea51",
                                                "sense_id": "d5b8898a-8fad-383e-b1dc-b5b761fd3aa4",
                                                "text": "Gisèle me demanda où elle pourrait la trouver, car elle avait justement quelque chose à lui dire. « Quoi donc ? — Des choses qui se rapportent à de petites camarades à elle. — Quelles camarades ? Je pourrai peut-être vous renseigner, ce qui ne vous empêchera pas de la voir. — Oh ! des camarades d’autrefois, je ne me rappelle pas les noms », répondit Gisèle d’un air vague, en battant en retraite. Elle me quitta, croyant avoir parlé avec une prudence telle que rien ne pouvait me paraître que très clair. Mais le mensonge est si peu exigeant, a besoin de si peu de chose pour se manifester ! S’il s’était agi de camarades d’autrefois, dont elle ne savait même pas les noms, pourquoi aurait-elle eu « justement » besoin d’en parler à Albertine ? Cet adverbe, assez parent d’une expression chère à Mme Cottard : « cela tombe à pic », ne pouvait s’appliquer qu’à une chose particulière, opportune, peut-être urgente, se rapportant à des êtres déterminés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "618350c8-1318-452e-a4a8-7b0fc55ff050",
                                                "sense_id": "d5b8898a-8fad-383e-b1dc-b5b761fd3aa4",
                                                "text": "— Tu veux que je téléphone de la cabine qui est en bas ? J’ai remarqué que, de la salle, on entend tout ce qui se dit…\n— Justement !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ba8554e-7011-365a-97ce-f671de966882",
                                        "entry_id": "63511c68-1d15-3282-8ec9-bbc5e0f13dc3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualifie qu'on vient de parler de telle ou telle chose/personne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36141ce3-e041-49e8-8456-1222f19c3d4c",
                                                "sense_id": "4ba8554e-7011-365a-97ce-f671de966882",
                                                "text": "Actuellement, l'équipe travaille beaucoup et de façon intense sur l'amélioration de l’Académie Français Authentique, dont Tom fait partie justement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
